ARTICLE IV — TRADE SECRET DECLARATION

The Work constitutes trade secrets of the Sovereign under:
  - Defend Trade Secrets Act, 18 U.S.C. § 1836 et seq.
  - Texas Uniform Trade Secrets Act, Tex. Civ. Prac. & Rem. Code § 134A

ItsNotAILABS has taken and continues to take reasonable measures to
maintain secrecy, including: access controls, confidentiality obligations,
technical protection measures, active AI surveillance (SAEIS), sovereign
token binding (Article XI), and this instrument.

Access to a publicly visible repository does not defeat trade secret
protection where, as here, the Sovereign has published clear notice of
proprietary status and deployed active enforcement mechanisms. See, e.g.,
Buffets, Inc. v. Klinke, 73 F.3d 965 (9th Cir. 1996); Penalty Kick Mgmt.
Ltd. v. Coca Cola Co., 318 F.3d 1284 (11th Cir. 2003).

