ARTICLE VII — ENFORCEMENT AND REMEDIES

Available remedies include, without limitation:

  CIVIL REMEDIES
  ─────────────
  (a) Preliminary and permanent injunctive relief without bond;
  (b) Actual damages including lost profits, reasonable royalties, and
      full disgorgement of unjust enrichment;
  (c) Statutory copyright damages up to $150,000 per work for willful
      infringement (17 U.S.C. § 504(c)(2));
  (d) DTSA exemplary damages up to 2× for willful misappropriation
      (18 U.S.C. § 1836(b)(3)(C));
  (e) Full attorneys' fees, costs, expert fees;
  (f) Disgorgement of all revenues, profits, and benefits from
      unauthorized use.

  CRIMINAL REFERRAL
  ─────────────────
  (g) 18 U.S.C. § 1832 — Theft of Trade Secrets (up to 10 years);
  (h) 18 U.S.C. § 1030 — Computer Fraud and Abuse Act;
  (i) Other applicable federal or state criminal statutes.

  TECHNICAL ENFORCEMENT (SAEIS)
  ──────────────────────────────
  (j) Token invalidation and access revocation;
  (k) Automated reporting to platform providers (GitHub DMCA, API ToS);
  (l) Cross-system organism enforcement via ItsNotAILABS internal
      infrastructure;
  (m) Evidence packaging from SAEIS logs for use in legal proceedings.

  NOTICE: SAEIS-flagged violations are automatically prepared for evidence
  submission. Willfulness is presumed where SAEIS logs confirm that the
  violating party accessed this instrument prior to the violation event.

