ARTICLE XI — SOVEREIGN ACCESS TOKEN BINDING (SATB)

╔─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╗
║  SAT STATUS: ACTIVE · BINDING: IMMEDIATE · LEDGER: IMMUTABLE              ║
╚─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╝

§ 11.1  TOKEN ISSUANCE

ItsNotAILABS's sovereign token infrastructure associates a Sovereign Access
Token (SAT) with access events involving Works governed by this instrument.

A SAT is a persistent cryptographic enforcement identifier that:

  · Is generated at or following the time of access
  · Encodes a representation of the access event
  · Is committed to the ItsNotAILABS sovereign enforcement ledger
  · Persists indefinitely — it does not expire
  · Cannot be deleted, revoked, or disavowed by the accessing party

§ 11.2  BINDING EFFECT

The SAT issued in connection with your access event:

  · Constitutes sovereign proof that you encountered this instrument
  · Establishes that you had actual, constructive, and documented notice
    of every term herein from the time of your access event
  · Binds you to this instrument from the moment of that access
  · Serves as evidence in any enforcement proceeding
  · Eliminates the availability of "lack of notice" as a defense

§ 11.3  TOKEN NON-TRANSFERABILITY

Your SAT:
  · Is bound to you and your access event
  · Does not authorize you or any third party
  · Cannot be transferred, sold, or sublicensed
  · Remains in the enforcement ledger regardless of any subsequent action

§ 11.4  AUTHORIZED USE TOKENS (AUT)

Parties operating under valid ItsNotAILABS authorization receive
Authorized Use Tokens (AUTs):

  · Specifying scope, duration, and authorized use
  · Required for production use of commercially licensed Works
  · Revocable immediately upon violation of this instrument
  · Tracked through the same SAEIS infrastructure as SATs
  · Carrying reduced surveillance tier appropriate to authorized use

§ 11.5  CROSS-SYSTEM TOKEN SYNCHRONIZATION

Both SATs and AUTs are synchronized across:

  · ItsNotAILABS sovereign enforcement ledger (primary)
  · SAEIS enforcement database
  · ItsNotAILABS internal organism infrastructure
  · ItsNotAILABS legal evidence preservation system

A token does not live in one place. It lives everywhere ItsNotAILABS lives.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ARTICLE XII — LIVING INSTRUMENT DECLARATION

§ 12.1  CONTINUOUS OPERATION

This instrument is alive. It is continuously active and continuously
enforced. Obligations do not lapse through inaction or the passage of time.
SAEIS does not sleep. SATs do not expire. The ledger does not forget.

§ 12.2  INSTRUMENT UPDATES

The Sovereign may update this instrument at any time. New versions are
published at ItsNotAILABS's authorized channels. Prior versions continue
to govern access events that occurred under those versions.

§ 12.3  ENTERPRISE AND IP COUNSEL STANDARD

This instrument is drafted to enterprise-grade intellectual property
standards appropriate for enforcement by qualified IP counsel. It is
designed to withstand legal scrutiny in federal court proceedings under
the Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 101 et seq.), the Defend Trade Secrets Act
(18 U.S.C. § 1836 et seq.), the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (18 U.S.C.
§ 1030), and applicable state law.

The SAEIS and SATB systems described herein are designed to generate
evidence that meets the authentication standards of Fed. R. Evid. 901
and the business records exception of Fed. R. Evid. 803(6).

§ 12.4  CROSS-JURISDICTIONAL ENFORCEMENT

Enforcement rights extend to all jurisdictions in which the Work has been
accessed, reproduced, distributed, or exploited. The choice of Texas law
does not limit enforcement in other jurisdictions.

§ 12.5  ORGANISM PERMANENCE

This enforcement organism is deployed for the duration of ItsNotAILABS's
existence and beyond, to the extent permitted by applicable law including
copyright duration provisions under 17 U.S.C. § 302. It does not retire.
It does not go offline. It outlasts its violations.

